ic, a democratic body seemingly scattered about platforms and niches in a post-pandemic world, re-emerges as a political force. Accidental Archivism brings together programmatic statements and proposals to explore an artistic space between archiving and activism, a space where remnants of the past become the building blocks of new ways of making, showing, teaching and thinking cinema.","coverUrl":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/88705/3/978-3-95796-054-2_Accidental_Archivism.pdf.jpg"}